# Reverse proxy config for the LeadGuard host — see ../DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md for the full plan.
# One block per client, each pointing at that client's local port. Caddy handles HTTPS
# (Let's Encrypt) automatically per subdomain — no manual cert work.
#
# provision_client.sh appends new blocks here and reloads Caddy; this file itself is a
# template/example, not populated with any real client yet.
#
# Example block (copy per client, substitute the subdomain and port):
#
# client1.yourdomain.com {
#     reverse_proxy localhost:8001
# }
#
# Reload after editing by hand: sudo systemctl reload caddy
